<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- RUT_Lightfall — the Forsaken Crags' one massive chasm (owner-named 2026-09-06:
       "where light falls in — the one place the Dark always dies";
       forsaken_crags.md §3). A distinct LandmarkDef, not a reskin of vanilla Chasm,
       because this is the singular deepest etch-scar on the planet — the Damp
       chain's terminator suture, ten thousand years of the Dark's collapse-rain
       eating one spot deepest. Reuses the vanilla Chasm icon (already repainted by
       mandrake.rut.ashkarrlandmarkart, World/Landmarks/Ashkarr/Chasm) rather than
       bespoke art: the owner left "what waits at the bottom" unwritten, so no new
       visual content is invented here — only the mechanism ruled in §3 (a chasm,
       the deepest one) is drawn.

       commonality 0 ON PURPOSE — worldgen must never roll it; it exists only to be
       force-placed on tile 9023 (MEASURED: hilliness 5, elev 919 m, current
       mutators Cliffs+HotSprings, no Chasm mutator yet) by the world-edit step this
       item still owes (jawa/world_landmarks_set + world_commit, LIGHTFALL_CHASM_
       AUTHORING_1, bridge work). mutatorChances carries Chasm Required="True" so
       placement adds the actual chasm mutator to the tile if it is not already
       there — same anchor vanilla Chasm and IshkoDarkLandmarks' RUT_ShadowedOverhang
       use. Description is present-tense, what IS: the scar and its cause, no
       not-yet-ruled content about what has been lowered into it. -->

  <LandmarkDef MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
    <defName>RUT_Lightfall</defName>
    <label>Lightfall</label>
    <description>The deepest etch on the whole planet — the one place, on the terminator suture where damp air meets the Dark, that the Dark has died longest. Ten thousand years of falling ash-grains, each one settling and dissolving a little more rock before the next clear pocket forms above the last, have eaten a chasm too deep to see the bottom of by lamp alone. Ropes, ladders, and worse have gone down over the years the way rumor always outruns confirmation; what any of them found is not something anyone who came back talks about.</description>
    <iconTexturePath>World/Landmarks/Ashkarr/Chasm</iconTexturePath>
    <atlasSize>(2, 2)</atlasSize>
    <commonality>0</commonality>
    <category>mountain</category>
    <mutatorChances>
      <Chasm Required="True"></Chasm>
    </mutatorChances>
    <nameMaker>NamerLandmark_Chasm</nameMaker>
  </LandmarkDef>

</Defs>
